Third-party files
=================

Adapters under adapters/ include files copied byte for byte from creators'
repositories, at the commit pinned in each adapter's vendored-upstream.json.
Those files keep their creators' copyright and licence. The MIT licence of this
repository does not cover them.

upstream-licences.json records, for every upstream an adapter copies files
from, its SPDX licence and where its licence text is: under licenses/<owner>/<repo>/
(fetched at the pinned commit) or beside the copied files in the adapter.
Neither sits inside a build context, so recording a licence never changes a
recipe or its image. Licences are informative; they never gate a recipe.

